# AL1 multimodal EEG-fMRI dataset

BRILLIANCE_AL1 EEG-fMRI dataset (visit 1), 34 participants

## Contents
- anat: defaced T1-weighted images (PyDeface 2.1.0 + FSL FLIRT 6.0).
  Only face voxels were zeroed/attenuated; brain voxels are untouched
  (verified against SPM12 unified-segmentation brain masks: 0 brain voxels
  changed in every subject). Images are defaced, not fully de-identified
  (ears and partial orbits remain).
- func: multiband BOLD, runs 1-2. RepetitionTime = 1300ms.
- eeg: EGI MFF recordings (.mff directories). MFF is not an accepted BIDS
  raw EEG format, so these are listed in .bidsignore and shared unmodified
  (except as noted under "EEG notes" for sub-034).
- derivatives/spm12-realign: SPM12 realignment parameters (rp_*.txt) for
  each BOLD run, where available.
- sourcedata/recall: per-participant EPRIME stimuli presentation log files (List A for visit 1) 

## Known missing data
- sub-007: T1 and recall file need to be refetched
- sub-049, sub-054: no realignment parameters (refetch)
- No DWI included (refetch later- talk to PK and confirm the final slurmjobdwis?).

## EEG notes
- sub-034: the source MFF package contained a redundant embedded copy of
  itself (an EGI re-save artifact). The embedded copy was verified to be a
  byte-identical duplicate of the outer recording (identical signal data
  and metadata; event file differing only in XML serialization) and was
  removed from this release. The outer recording is complete and unaltered.
- sub-055: the MFF package is an EEGLAB re-export. Its event markers are in
  Events_exported_from_EEGLAB_2.xml and Events_exported_from_EEGLAB_3.xml
  rather than the ECI event-track file present for other participants, and
  acquisition-software files (e.g., recordingSettings.xml) are absent.


